From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: input layouts with registers left out

An input layout may leave out the registers its shader doesn't read; gallium's vertex elements are indexed by
register, so a gap was an element of format NONE, which virglrenderer refuses (VIRGL_ERROR_CTX_ILLEGAL_VERTEX_FORMAT):
the layout wasn't created and the draws used the one bound before. GravityMark's Direct3D 11 asteroid shadow casters
(v0 and v3 only) read their positions in another layout's format, misplaced in the shadow map: the Earth's day side
was in shadow. A gap is now one float from a buffer the layout already reads, which the shader never does.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/InputAssembly.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/InputAssembly.cpp
index d94ac5e..115878a 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/InputAssembly.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/InputAssembly.cpp
@@ -312,9 +312,16 @@ CreateElementLayout(
       max_elements = MAX2(max_elements, pVertexElement->InputRegister + 1);
    }
 
-   /* XXX: What do we do when there's a gap? */
-   if (max_elements != num_elements) {
-      DebugPrintf("%s: gap\n", __func__);
+   /* Registers the shader doesn't read may be left out (GravityMark's asteroid shadows: v0 and v3), but gallium's
+    * elements are indexed by register: a gap is an element of no format, and virglrenderer fails a layout with one,
+    * so the draws kept the previous layout (another position format: shadow casters misplaced, the Earth's day side
+    * in shadow). A gap gets one float from a buffer the layout reads; the shader never does. */
+   for (unsigned i = 0; i < max_elements; i++) {
+      struct pipe_vertex_element *ve = &pElementLayout->state.velems[i];
+      if (ve->src_format == PIPE_FORMAT_NONE) {
+         ve->src_format = PIPE_FORMAT_R32_FLOAT;
+         ve->vertex_buffer_index = pCreateElementLayout->pVertexElements[0].InputSlot;
+      }
    }
 
    pElementLayout->state.count = max_elements;
